From 34a22585ffdab6a04b3e64d196fcc6c42ac9b7ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:43:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: start the enhancement layer by picture order
 only where it can be known

By picture order, the layer starts at a random-access picture of both
layers with the same picture order count in one packet, or at a place that
rank_try() counts from a random-access picture of the base layer. The fork
also took an IDR picture of the layer alone for the base picture of its
packet where the base layer "does not reorder", which it knew from
has_b_frames of the context the module made of the stream's parameters:
a number read once, from the configuration the stream was opened with (0
without one, where the parameter sets come in the packets: FFmpeg's
decoder only reads it from extradata) and never again. And that placement
is right only for an IDR picture without leading pictures. Where the base
layer reorders and that number reads 0, the layer started at the base
picture of the packet, another picture than its own, and every picture
after it was paired with a neighbour's: the one start that did not fail
closed.

The shortcut is gone. Its one right case, an IDR picture of the layer in
a base layer that does not reorder, is a place that rank_try() counts:
from the identities the base pictures have, whatever the stream says of
its reordering, with the leading pictures of both layers, and given up
when it cannot be known. Where Kodi opens a stream with a configuration
whose SPS says that the base layer reorders (Matroska and MP4 files of
Blu-ray streams), the shortcut was off already, and nothing changes.

Measured on the host (fel_rpu_test, as Kodi): the module reads 0 for the
FEL test stream as the test opens it, so the shortcut was in force in its
runs; the whole file, nine starts in the middle and two seeks, each also
with the reordering made 0 by hand, give the same pictures, byte for byte,
before and after, every one paired with its own enhancement picture. None
of the streams at hand has an IDR picture of the layer away from a
random-access picture of the base layer with the same picture order
count, so no run shows the wrong start: that it could happen is read in
the code (not verified on a stream).
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
index 62b034e..e4604ed 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
@@ -846,7 +846,8 @@ static void rank_base(struct dvbridge_fel *f, int type, int64_t identity)
  * each in every packet, the picture j is presented at the place
  *     (j - b) + leading(j) - leading(b)
  * among the base pictures presented from b on, counted from 0. Where the base layer does not reorder its pictures
- * and j is an IDR picture, that is the base picture of the packet of j (el_idr in dvbridge_fel_submit()).
+ * and j is an IDR picture without leading pictures, that is the base picture of the packet of j (which the fork took
+ * as such where the stream's parameters said that the base layer does not reorder: dvbridge_fel_submit()).
  *
  * The base pictures are known by their picture order, which is the order they are presented in. The place is
  * read as an identity only when every identity from the one of b to it has come, in the step that the identities
@@ -1541,13 +1542,20 @@ bool dvbridge_fel_submit(struct dvbridge_fel *f, const AVPacket *packet)
         else if (f->synchronizing) {
             const AVCodecParserContext *bp = f->base_order.parser;
             const AVCodecParserContext *ep = f->enhancement_order.parser;
-            bool common_key = bp->key_frame == 1 && ep->key_frame == 1 &&
-                              bp->output_picture_number == ep->output_picture_number;
-            /* A non-reordered BL gives the IDR packet an unambiguous display
-             * time. Never use this shortcut for a BL with reordered pictures. */
-            bool el_idr = ep->key_frame == 1 && ep->output_picture_number == 0 &&
-                          f->base_order.context->has_b_frames == 0;
-            if (common_key || el_idr) {
+            /* A random-access picture of both layers, with the same picture order count, in the same packet: the
+             * same picture.
+             * Hades: and nothing else starts the layer here. The fork also took an IDR picture of the layer alone
+             * for the base picture of its packet where the base layer "does not reorder", which it knew from the
+             * has_b_frames of the stream's parameters: a number read once, from the configuration the stream was
+             * opened with (0 without one, where the parameter sets come in the packets) and never again, and that
+             * placement is right only for an IDR picture of the layer without leading pictures. With a base layer
+             * that reorders and that number read as 0, the layer started at the base picture of the packet, another
+             * picture than its own, and every picture after it was paired with a neighbour's. That start is the place
+             * that rank_try() counts, below: from the identities the base pictures have, whatever the stream says of
+             * its reordering, with the leading pictures of both layers, and given up when it cannot be known. */
+            const bool common_key = bp->key_frame == 1 && ep->key_frame == 1 &&
+                                    bp->output_picture_number == ep->output_picture_number;
+            if (common_key) {
                 /* Hades: a random-access picture of the layer whose place was being counted gives way
                  * to this one; the access units passed over since the last IDR picture of the layer
                  * take the identities of their base pictures from here, for their RPUs. */
-- 
